course: dictionary
lesson: 6060
title: Merciful and mercifully
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Merciful is an adjective. It describes someone who is kind and forgiving, especially to a person they could punish or hurt. In the sentence «It begins with the Beatitudes, blessings for people the world often overlooks: the poor in spirit, those who mourn, the meek, the merciful, the pure in heart and the peacemakers», the list names kinds of good people, so merciful describes someone kind and forgiving.
explain: Use a clue to check. Ask: what would a person who is not merciful do? They would punish or hurt someone who had done wrong. A merciful person chooses to forgive instead. Swap your meaning into the list: «the forgiving» fits well, so your meaning works.
explain: The word also has a religious meaning. Christians believe God is merciful, forgiving people who are sorry. Muslims call God «the Most Merciful». Some religion lessons quote «Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy».
explain: Merciful can also mean bringing relief from something bad, as in «a merciful release» or «mercifully short». Mercifully is the adverb, so «The lesson was mercifully short» means the lesson was short, and that was a relief.
fact: Merciful is an adjective: merciful, more merciful, most merciful.
fact: «Merciful» means kind and forgiving to someone you could punish or harm.
fact: «Mercifully» is the adverb form, as in «mercifully short».
fact: Christians believe God is merciful, forgiving people who are sorry.
fact: Muslims call God «the Most Merciful», and this phrase begins most chapters of the Qur'an.
exercise: «Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy.» What does merciful mean here? | *Kind and forgiving | Very tired after a long day | Loud and proud | Quick to run away
exercise: In a story, a merciful king spares his enemy. What did the king do? | He challenged his enemy to a race | He hid from his enemy | He gave his enemy a bigger army | *He did not harm his enemy
exercise: Find and copy the adverb in «The storm was mercifully short.» | short | was | *mercifully | storm
test: «The judge was merciful and let the boy go with a warning.» What does merciful mean? | Quick and loud | *Kind and forgiving, not harsh | Angry and strict | Hungry and tired
test: Sam says the king is «more merciful» than his brother. What does this mean? | *He is kinder and more forgiving than his brother | He is louder than his brother | He is more tired than his brother | He is taller than his brother
exam: Muslims call God «the Most Merciful». What does this title tell us about God? | That God is the most hungry | That God is the most loud | That God is the most tired | *That God is the most kind and forgiving
